  ▶ $ cd ~/work/yoyo-evolve/yoyo-evolve; gh issue view 1047 --json… (5 lines) ✓ (1.1s)

read_file no longer hangs on a FIFO. It now refuses FIFOs, character and block devices (like /dev/null or a tty) and sockets before the underlying tool opens them. Build, the full test suite, clippy and fmt all pass, and it's committed as 2a5ab792 under the title "Part of #1047".

What changed
• New module `src/non_regular_read.rs`. It looks at the path's file type without opening it. Regular files, symlinks to regular files, directories and missing paths are left alone. Directories already fail fast with "Is a directory", and a missing path keeps the tool's own error, so those cases behave exactly as before. Anything else gets an error saying what kind of file it is and why it's refused.
• Wiring: one call each in GuardedTool and ArcGuardedTool in src/tool_wrappers.rs. Both wrap every read_file whether or not --allow-dir/--deny-dir is set, so the main agent and sub-agents both get the check. tool_wrappers.rs went from 5684 to 5692 lines, and I updated its entry in the size register (tests/module_size.rs).
• Docs: a new section in docs/src/troubleshooting/common-issues.md.

Verification
• Unit tests cover a FIFO (the test first confirms the fixture really is a FIFO), /dev/null, a regular file, a symlink to a regular file, a missing path and a directory.
• A second test calls the wrapped tool the way production builds it, with no fence set, for both wrapper types.
• My first version of that test hung instead of failing. tokio::time::timeout can't catch this hang because the stuck read runs on a blocking thread that the test runtime waits for at shutdown. The test now runs the call on a separate thread with a 10s cutoff.
• With the wiring removed, the FIFO test fails by name after 10s; with it put back, it passes. I did both in one command so the removal couldn't be left in.
• End to end: I re-ran the assessment's repro (mkfifo pipe.txt plus a -p run asking for read_file pipe.txt) with the built binary. It finished with exit 0 in 15s and the model reported the refusal; before, the same run was killed at 80s with exit 124.

Still open on #1047 (I listed these in a comment on the issue): the REPL /add and @path readers, which don't go through read_file and haven't been tested against a FIFO, and the fix in yoagent itself. I didn't file a yoagent issue.
